>I've been trying to figure out a strategy for getting the Amulet of
>Yendor away from the Wiz without having to kill him. I know one can
>polymorph into a nymph and steel it from him, but I'd prefer avoiding
>that. It occurred to me that I could zap him with a teleport ray
>while he was sleeping on the Amulet.  He and the amulet would be
>separately teleported to other random parts of the maze. I then would
>use an object detect potion or crystal ball to locate the amulet.
>Then I teleport myself to where it is, grab it, and head for the
>stairway, using paralysis potions to slow the Wiz down. then I'm out
>of that level and free from the Wiz's random attacks and item-
>cursing.  Can anyone out there test out this strategy? Maybe someone
>on a mac or PC whose copying his save files?

It should work.  The thing you would have to be most careful of is
silence.  Stepping on a squeaky board or setting off a land mine would
wake the Wizard, and the first thing he would do is grab the Amulet.
I'm not sure, but I think a pick-axe would also be too noisy.  Keep a
wand of digging handy, just in case.  Potions of paralysis, by the
way, are very nice in handling the Wizard (in this version; in the
next this 'feature' should be gone).  
Bigger spoilers ahead...

The trick goes like this: Get the Amulet, then throw the potion at the
Wizard.  He must be paralyzed, not slain.  Teleport to the staircase
immediately and run (don't walk) the rest of the way.  See, paralysis
counters are only incremented for monsters on your level.  If the
Wizard is still paralyzed when you leave the level, he will remain so
until you return.  On other monsters this doesn't matter, since the
Wizard is the only one which will follow you across levels after being
slain.

>Some other miscellaneous questions:
>What is the lowest AC a character may have before value wrap-around occurs?
> My guy is at AC -48 on NH 3.0j on a Sun machine...

The lowest AC a character may have is -128.  (or is it -127?  close enough...)

>Is there a maximum number of items that can be put in a bag o'holding before 
>something terrible happens, esp. when using the curse/bless bug to expand its
>capacity?

Not really.  Bags of holding don't completely negate the weight of the
items inside, though, so you're still limited by your own carrying
capacity.

>What items should not go in a bag o' holding?

The Amulet cannot be placed in any container (bag, box or chest).
Wands of cancellation and other bags will cause a bag of holding to explode.

